«
    @ SciRngRnd: round a measured value and its uncertainty by the NIST rule:
    @ the uncertainty to 2 significant digits, the value to the same decimal place.
    @ Accepts a±b, a±σb, a±p%, a…b, with or without units, or two values X U.
    @ Returns the same type. A zero uncertainty leaves the value unchanged.
    @ After Jean Wilson's SciRngRnd (2025-2026).

    @ Rounding core: X U → Xr Ur, both plain numbers in the same unit
    «
        IF DUP 0 = THEN
        ELSE
            -2 RND DUP UNROT StdRnd SWAP
        END
    »
    @ Split a value from its unit: Obj → Value 1_unit (or 1 without unit)
    «
        IF DUP TypeName "unit" == THEN
            DUP UVAL SWAP 1 SWAP →Unit
        ELSE
            1
        END
    »
    → SciCore SciSplit
    «
        IF DUP TypeName "unit" == THEN DUP UVAL ELSE DUP END
        TypeName → SciKind
        «
            IF SciKind "drange" == SciKind "uncertain" == OR
               SciKind "prange" == OR SciKind "range" == OR
            THEN
                @ One interval: separate its unit, then its two components
                SciSplit SWAP Object→
                CASE
                    SciKind "drange" == THEN SciCore →∆Range END
                    SciKind "uncertain" == THEN SciCore →σRange END
                    SciKind "prange" == THEN
                        → Xc Pc
                        « Xc Xc ABS Pc × 100 ÷ SciCore DROP Pc -2 RND →%Range »
                    END
                    @ range: centre and half-width, rounded, then bounds again
                    → Lo Hi
                    « Lo Hi + 2 ÷ Hi Lo - 2 ÷ SciCore
                      → Xc Ux « Xc Ux - Xc Ux + →Range » »
                END
                ×
            ELSE
                @ Two values X U: express U in the unit of X, then round as a±b
                IF OVER TypeName "unit" == THEN
                    IF DUP TypeName "unit" == THEN OVER Convert END
                END
                SciSplit DROP SWAP SciSplit UNROT SWAP
                SciCore →∆Range ×
            END
        »
    »
»
